{
  "created": "2026-10-19T14:00:21.936300+02:00",
  "feature": "Event encoder mixins and explicit delivery without Contract.emit",
  "api": {
    "record": "class Mint(Event, Bytesrepr): ...",
    "defaultEncoder": "event.to_message()",
    "explicitEncoder": "Json.to_message(event)",
    "nativeDelivery": "runtime.emit_message(topic, event.to_message())",
    "cesDelivery": "ces.emit(event, events=Contract.event_types())",
    "cesInstallation": "ces.initial_named_keys(events) / ces.initialize(events)",
    "customEncoder": "class Custom(MessageEncoder): ..."
  },
  "behavior": [
    "One encoder supplies the default; zero or multiple encoders raise TypeError",
    "Records can override to_message to define a default",
    "All encoder mixins return MessageString | MessageBytes for compatible typing",
    "Bytesrepr encodes ordered fields without the CES event-name envelope",
    "Json returns text; JsonBytes returns UTF-8 JSON in a binary carrier",
    "Event has no to_bytes or to_json methods and imposes no decoder",
    "CES framing and state are owned by cspr.ces; Contract has no emit API",
    "JSON field validation does not produce a binary field payload",
    "The freezer binds constructors and encoder choices without executing source",
    "Inheritance with incompatible MicroPython lookup is rejected",
    "All nine upstream CEP-18 CES payloads, schemas and native messages remain compatible"
  ],
